# <%= current_page.data.title %>

## Purpose

Make sure support and enquiry emails are noticed, followed up, and dealt with properly, even when a different person handles the mailbox each day. The goal is to keep the process simple and easy to manage.


## Who's Responsible

The assigned daily support person is responsible for checking and managing emails in the shared mailbox throughout their shift.


## Daily Workflow

| Time | Task |
|------|------|
| **Start of day** | Open shared mailbox in Outlook and review unread messages. |
| **Triage each email** | Categorize using agreed tags (see below), mark clearly if action is needed. |
| **Action what you can** | Respond or assign via Slack/GitHub project board. |
| **Flag if needs follow-up** | Use a ⏳ **Waiting** category and note who owns it. |
| **Archive emails** | Move the emails that are completed or marked as **Done** to the archive folder. |
| **End of day** | Reply to any unacknowledged sender with a holding message if needed, and hand over if something is unresolved. |

## Categories

- 🔧 **Support Request** – Help with platform.
- 💬 **General Enquiry** – Informational, non-urgent.
- 🚨 **Escalate** – Needs PM, DM or Service Owner.
- ✅ **Done** – Resolved and replied to.
- ⏳ **Waiting** – Awaiting input from others.

## 🧾 Email Handling Guidelines

- Acknowledge all emails within **1 working day**.
- Log trackable requests in **GitHub Project**: If an email relates to a new feature request, bug, or a task that requires follow-up or input from others, create a ticket in the appropriate board.
- Escalate unclear issues to the **PM, DM or Service Owner**.
- Archive only after resolving (**do not delete unless it's spam**).

## 📢 Holding Message Template

> Hi \<Name>,
>
> Thanks for your email. I've picked this up and will get back to you shortly, or loop in someone who can help.
>
> Kind Regards,
> Support Developer
